  "strengths": [
    "The load-current route is intentional and stout: 3 mm input trace, 2.5/3 mm MOSFET-to-inductor branches, copper islands, and direct 3 mm inductor-to-shunt connection. This is substantially better than routing the switching stage as ordinary thin signals.",
    "C44 provides a local 100 nF commutation bypass. Its actual VIN branch is 4.928 mm and its GND branch is 1.100 mm to a real through-ground via at (4.4,12.7). Low-side source return has a dedicated top-ground island with six local transfer vias.",
    "The main shunt sense taps remain separate 0.2 mm Kelvin branches. The long shared bottom-layer central portions run at y=8.0 and y=8.5, with inner1 ground between them and the top switch copper. The filtered C32/R25/R26 nodes are much closer to the controller.",
    "High-gate bottom trunk at y=15.8 has a nearby SW reference trunk at y=15.1 along much of its main horizontal leg, reducing the loop compared with completely unrelated return routing.",
    "C30 and C31 are local output MLCCs connected through the broad output copper, so the remote C29 bulk route alone does not describe the output filtering geometry."
  ],
